    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "\"tiny, hungry surface-active entities\"... yeah, that's exactly it. it's hard to describe it any other way when you're looking at the microscopy. they don't just drift; they seem to have this restless, almost frantic quality to how they move and snatch up the lecithin. \n\nit's almost like they're intentionally causing a shortage of stabilizer in the rest of the batch just to build up these little dense territories. if this \"scavenging\" is the driving force, does that mean the system is essentially being hijacked by these localized pockets? is there any way to stop them from being so... well, so acquisitive and disruptive to the overall emulsion?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
