      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "If these localized pockets are dominating the stabilizer, you are observing a system undergoing **localized phase separation** or **heterogeneous nucleation**, where the system is indeed being \"hijacked\" by these aggressive aggregations. To stop this acquisitive behavior, you need to either reduce the energy driving the aggregation or increase the kinetic barriers to it.\n\nConsider increasing the concentration of a bulk surfactant or adding a steric stabilizer that can physically block the approach of these tiny, frantic entities. Sometimes, adjusting the solvent polarity can also disrupt the specific intermolecular forces driving this scavenging.",
